Q: How to convert Date or String to time in Hexadecimal I want to convert a Date or String to Hexadecimal Time. 
Here is the piece of code I am currently using:
  var hexDateTimeString = "";

  try {
      hexDateTimeString = convert(DateTime.Now, DateTime.Now.Hour.ToString("X2"), DateTime.Now.Minute.ToString("X2") , DateTime.Now.Second.ToString("X2"));    
  } 
  catch (System.Exception ex) {
      //Handle exception...    
  }

  public string convert(object objDateTime, object objHour, object objMinute, object objSecond)
  {
    string strDateTimeString = objDateTime.ToString();
    string strHour = objHour.ToString();
    string strMinute = objMinute.ToString();
    string strSecond = objSecond.ToString();

    string strHexDateTimeString = string.Format("{0}{1}{2}{3}", strHour, strMinute, strSecond);
    return strHexDateTimeString;
  }

My code is successfully returning a hexadecimal representation of the current hour but is throwing an error when I try to add minutes and seconds to it. 

System.InvalidCastException: 'Specified cast is not valid.'

This is because "objHour" is not being correctly parsed by the "ToString("X2")" method. Instead of providing a 2-character Hex representation, it appears to be returning it as '02' where as I need it to act as '2' because if I use it in a hex number computation, if would equal 32 not 2.
How can I correct my code and also return the time in Hexadecimal, without having the hour be displayed double digits (like '02' instead of '2'). I need to output it as a '2' instead of '02' representation.

A: Your issue is because you expect all the parameters (hour, minute and second) to be strings. Instead, it seems like the hour is being parsed to an integer. You can fix it by converting the parameters to strings with ToString("X2") before calling the conversion function.
You can also reduce your code complexity by removing the explicit variables.
Here is the correction of your code:
try
{
    hexDateTimeString = convert(DateTime.Now.ToString("HHmmss"));
}
catch (System.Exception ex)
{
    //Handle exception
}

public string convert(string input)
{
    return input;
}

Here, you simply convert your DateTime to a 6-char string representation (HH=24hr format), which will already be a 'hexadecimal' formatted string.

