## How do I enable the Pex feature of Fuzzing?

To enable the Fuzzing feature of Pex, follow these steps:

1. Install Visual Studio 2015 or Update 1 if you have a different version of Visual Studio installed.
2. Navigate to Tools > Extensions and Updates.
3. Search for "Pex - Re-engineer Unit Tests in Visual Studio."
4. Click Install.
5. Once installed, open your C# project where you want to apply Fuzzing feature. In the Solution Explore, right-click the unit test project and choose "Add>New Item".
6. From the New Item dialog, choose "Pex Attribute Considered User Code". Under this new item, a `PexClass` attribute should be added to your new unit test class.

Your test class should look something like this:

```csharp
[PexClass(typeof(SomeClassToTest))]
public class SomeClassToTestPex
{
    // Pex will start fuzzing tests from here
}
``` 

You can then start to add fuzz tests by simply adding a method and using the Pex attributes. For example, you could add a method like this:

```csharp
[PexMethod]
public int Add(int a, int b)
{
    return a + b;
}
```

Pex will then automatically generate several tests including boundary, equivalence, and randomized tests. 

There are plenty of other attributes and features available in Pex, so you can learn more by browsing the [MSDN documentation](https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/mt184409.aspx){:target="_blank"}

{% include links.html %}






































































































































































































































































































































































































































































































