[n--------------------            Debug.Assert(
                ((Old_arrListLastIndexOfX == -1) && New_Ret == false) ||
                ((Old_arrListLastIndexOfX == -1) && New_Ret == true) ||
                ((Old_arrListLastIndexOfX >= -1) && New_Ret == false) ||
                ((Old_arrListLastIndexOfX >= -1) && New_Ret == true), 
                "This is because a new element is being added to the array list.");

            // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ If the return value is true and old index of x is > -1, the new index is also greater than -1.
            Debug.Assert(
                (Old_arrListIndexOfX > -1 && New_Ret == true) == (New_arrListIndexOfX > -1), 
                "This is because we've just added x to arrList, so the index of x should be greater than -1 in arrList.");

        }
    }
}
```

This test uses ArrayList's `Contains` method in an assertion and verifies that if the method returns true then the element is present in the list.

## Conclusion

In this article, we discussed using the PexLib's PexContract attribute for automated conformance verification. We studied how PexContract can aid in testing the internal behavior of algorithms and the structure of data types, providing a tool to test the correctness of the algorithms as they act upon the data types. It's valuable at all levels of your program testing: unit, integration, and system testing.

For more information about Pex, you can visit the Official Microsoft Research page using [this link](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/project/partial-evaluation-tool-for-net/).

Happy coding.

### Further Reading

1. [Understanding and using Pex Tool](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/visualstudio/test/using-pex-to-test-your-code?view=vs-2019) - Microsoft Documentation

2. [How to use Pex to test your code](https://www.codeproject.com/Articles/595368/Using-Pex-to-Test-Your-Code) - CodeProject Article

3. [Quick Start Guide to Pex](https://www.codeproject.com/Articles/119331/Quick-Start-Guide-to-Pex) - CodeProject Article

4. [PexLib](https://github.com/dennisgutierrez/PexLib) - GitHub Repository contains sample unit tests and contracts.

